{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfrwAixy7fqLnWhcTNrCn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Packages pinned in the constraints file are now exempt from the `--max-release-age` filter, so a pin like `boto3==1.35.88` resolves in both single-version and multi-version bootstrap mode. `tests/test_cooldown.py` and `tests/test_resolver.py` pass (71 tests). I didn't run ruff or mypy, because `ruff` isn't installed in `.venv`.\n\n**Fix** (`src/fromager/resolver.py`, in `find_all_matching_from_provider`):\n- **Behaviour:** when the provider's constraints have an entry for the package, the age filter is skipped and an info log says the package is pinned by constraint.\n- **Multi-version mode:** the pin is no longer emptied out by the filter, so resolution succeeds.\n- **Single-version mode:** the misleading \"keeping all to avoid empty resolution\" warning no longer appears for pinned packages.\n- **Docstring:** I added a line noting that `max_age_cutoff` is ignored for constrained packages.\n\n**Regression test:** `test_max_release_age_skipped_for_constrained_package` in `tests/test_cooldown.py`, run with the fallback both on and off. It pins `test-pkg==1.2.2` (84 days old) under a 30-day window and checks that `1.2.2` is returned with no \"keeping all\" warning. I also added the `constraints` import to that file.\n\nI didn't commit anything. Skipping the filter applies to any package that has a constraint entry, not only exact `==` pins."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7880,"cache_read_input_tokens":67802,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7880},"output_tokens":502,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ae5cc280-7d28-40ae-a8ce-0bccc8a4e8